      "title": "INCY Q3 Loss Narrower Than Expected, Sales Beat, FY'26 View Raised",
      "summary": "Incyte Corporation reported Q3 2026 revenues of $1.56 billion, up 14% year-over-year and beating estimates, despite posting an adjusted loss of $3.60 per share due to acquisition-related R&D expenses. Key products Opzelura, Niktimvo, and Zynyz showed strong growth. The company raised its 2026 net sales guidance to $5.21-$5.30 billion, reflecting continued commercial momentum.",
